<%#
  Common settings — Replay (issue #992 split). Emits items only.
%>
<sdpi-item label="Replay jump playback">
  <sdpi-select setting="replayJumpPlayback" global default="remember">
    <option value="remember">Remember state</option>
    <option value="play">Play</option>
    <option value="stopped">Stopped</option>
  </sdpi-select>
</sdpi-item>
<div class="ird-supporting-text">
  What the replay does after Replay Control's "Jump to Fastest Lap" or "Jump to
  Green Flag", or a Replay Markers "Previous / Next Marker" jump, has landed.
  <strong>Remember state</strong>
  carries on exactly as before the press: paused stays paused, and normal speed,
  slow motion, fast-forward and rewind continue at the same speed from the new
  spot. <strong>Play</strong> always plays at normal speed. <strong>Stopped</strong>
  always pauses on the new spot.
</div>
<sdpi-item label="Fastest Lap Search Delay (ms)">
  <ird-range-input setting="fastestLapSearchDelayMs" min="50" max="1000" step="50" default="400" global showlabels></ird-range-input>
</sdpi-item>
<div class="ird-supporting-text">
  Time the Replay Control "Jump to Fastest Lap" mode waits between each lap-search
  broadcast when it has to search the replay — a lap iRaceDeck recorded live is a
  single jump and needs no search. iRacing resolves the exact lap-boundary
  position asynchronously after each step, so a too-short delay can leave the
  cursor parked mid-lap; each step may also take up to four times this value to
  settle before the search gives up, and the single jump to a recorded lap at
  least three seconds. "Jump to Green Flag" uses the same delay when it has to
  search the replay for the race start. Default 400 ms. Slower computers and
  longer tracks may need to increase the value.
</div>
